<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dhulbahante</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dhulbahante are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> clan of the Harti branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darod">Darod</a>, living mainly in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sool">Sool</a> region and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanaag">Sanaag</a> and Togdheer. Their territory lies within the borders of former British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a>, but many Dhulbahante have rejected the authority of Somaliland, and their lands have been contested between Somaliland, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puntland">Puntland</a> and, from 2023, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ssc-khatumo">SSC-Khatumo</a> administration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dhulbahante.jpg" alt="Dhulbahante" width="311" height="342" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown Author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D9%85%D8%AD%D9%85%D9%91%D8%AF_%D8%B9%D8%A8%D8%AF_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%84%D9%91%D9%87_%D8%AD%D8%B3%D9%86.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
